{"content":[{"c":["NAHOR (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Abraham’s grandfather (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.11.22-25","r":"Gen.11.22-25","rawR":"Gen.11.22-25","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.11.22-25","value":"Gen.11.22-25"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 11:22-25"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.1.26","r":"1Chr.1.26","rawR":"1Chr.1.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.1.26","value":"1Chr.1.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 1:26"},"); also an ancestor of Jesus according to Luke’s genealogy (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.34","r":"Luke.3.34","rawR":"Luke.3.34","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.34","value":"Luke.3.34"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:34"},", where some English translations follow the Greek spelling, Nachor). The Genesis and 1 Chronicles passages show that Nahor is from Shem’s line. Hence, Abraham and his descendants are part of the Semitic family of nations."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Son of Terah and Abraham’s brother (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.11.26-29","r":"Gen.11.26-29","rawR":"Gen.11.26-29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.11.26-29","value":"Gen.11.26-29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 11:26-29"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.24.2","r":"Josh.24.2","rawR":"Josh.24.2","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.24.2","value":"Josh.24.2"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 24:2"},"). He married Milcah, Haran’s daughter, and his family is named in ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.22.20-23","r":"Gen.22.20-23","rawR":"Gen.22.20-23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.22.20-23","value":"Gen.22.20-23"}],"t":"ref","v":"Genesis 22:20-23"},". Abraham sent his servant to seek a wife for Isaac at Nahor’s residence in Mesopotamia (see ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.24.10","r":"Gen.24.10","rawR":"Gen.24.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.24.10","value":"Gen.24.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 24:10"},", which possibly suggests that the city itself was called Nahor). There he found Rebekah, Nahor’s granddaughter (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.24.1-51","r":"Gen.24.1-51","rawR":"Gen.24.1-51","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.24.1-51","value":"Gen.24.1-51"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 24:1-51"},"). Nahor is also named as the father (perhaps grandfather) of Laban, to whom Jacob went when he fled from his brother Esau (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.29.5","r":"Gen.29.5","rawR":"Gen.29.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.29.5","value":"Gen.29.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 29:5"},"). Both of these texts link Abraham’s family with related Semitic people. In ",{"href":"?bref=Gen.31.53","r":"Gen.31.53","rawR":"Gen.31.53","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.31.53","value":"Gen.31.53"}],"t":"ref","v":"Genesis 31:53"}," God is spoken of as “the God of Abraham and Nahor.”"],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":[{"c":["See also"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=NahorPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"NahorPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"NahorPlace_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Nahor (Place)"},"."],"sourceClass":"list-text","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"NahorPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 11:22-25","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.11.22-25","rawQueryValue":"Gen.11.22-25","sourceRefExact":"Gen.11.22-25"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 1:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.1.26","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.1.26","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.1.26"},{"anchorText":"Lk 3:34","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.3.34","rawQueryValue":"Luke.3.34","sourceRefExact":"Luke.3.34"},{"anchorText":"Gn 11:26-29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.11.26-29","rawQueryValue":"Gen.11.26-29","sourceRefExact":"Gen.11.26-29"},{"anchorText":"Jos 24:2","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.24.2","rawQueryValue":"Josh.24.2","sourceRefExact":"Josh.24.2"},{"anchorText":"Genesis 22:20-23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.22.20-23","rawQueryValue":"Gen.22.20-23","sourceRefExact":"Gen.22.20-23"},{"anchorText":"Gn 24:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.24.10","rawQueryValue":"Gen.24.10","sourceRefExact":"Gen.24.10"},{"anchorText":"Gn 24:1-51","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.24.1-51","rawQueryValue":"Gen.24.1-51","sourceRefExact":"Gen.24.1-51"},{"anchorText":"Gn 29:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.29.5","rawQueryValue":"Gen.29.5","sourceRefExact":"Gen.29.5"},{"anchorText":"Genesis 31:53","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.31.53","rawQueryValue":"Gen.31.53","sourceRefExact":"Gen.31.53"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"c22936350c7de950c5e45265fd68c02b28c507d223c4e251522e20867e2c44e1","sourceItemName":"NahorPerson","sourceItemOrder":33,"sourceMember":"Articles/N.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"NahorPerson","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Nahor (Person)","title":"Nahor (Person)","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}